Here's the semantic interpretation of the scene images in the requested RDF triples format, followed by the identified risks.

Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Nighttime encounter with unusual activity" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;  # Assuming the two figures are pedestrians
:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision with pedestrians in unusual positions" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

